      "sequence_position": 10,
      "problem": "Given the vectors $u=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$, find the distance $\\text{d}(u,v).$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the distance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(u,v) & =‖u-v‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({u}_{1}-{v}_{1})^{2}+({u}_{2}-{v}_{2})^{2}+({u}_{3}-{v}_{3})^{2}+({u}_{4}-{v}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4-(-2))^{2}+(0-(-3))^{2}+(1-1)^{2}+(7-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+9+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
